## 10. Extensions and recommendations

1. **Window-robust inference:** add Rossi–Inoue window-robust OOS tests ([2012](https://doi.org/10.1080/07350015.2012.663261)) and Harvey–Leybourne–Newbold small-sample DM adjustment ([1997](https://doi.org/10.1016/S0169-2070(96)00719-4)).
2. **Forecast-set comparison:** replace pairwise selection by the Model Confidence Set ([Hansen, Lunde & Nason 2011](https://doi.org/10.3982/ECTA5771)).
3. **Density:** skew-$t$ / GJR-GARCH, realized-variance regressors (HAR; [Corsi 2009](https://doi.org/10.1093/jjfinec/nbp001)), Berkowitz tests, conditional-coverage tests, and parameter-uncertainty bootstrap.
4. **Joint scenario generation:** bootstrap *rows* of $(r_t,x_t)$ in blocks ([Künsch 1989](https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1176347265), [Politis & Romano 1994](https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870)) to retain the target–drive dependence; build a multivariate (e.g. copula/DCC; [Bollerslev, Chou & Kroner 1992](https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-4076(92)90064-X)) model for the three-asset dashboard.
5. **Selection stability:** report stability-selection frequencies ([Meinshausen & Bühlmann 2010](https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9868.2010.00740.x)).
6. **Purged CV** with embargo for overlapping targets.
7. **Asset-specific drives:** FX — rate differentials, intervention proxies; Brent — term-structure slope/inventories; Gold — real yields. Use roll-adjusted Brent futures.
8. **Reporting:** make the dashboard's cautionary text conditional on the actual CW/KS/CUSUM results.

